    question: 'What is two-factor authentication (2FA)?',
    answer: '<p>Two-factor authentication adds a second layer of security beyond your password. Even if someone steals your password, they can\'t access your account without the second factor—usually a code from your phone or a physical key.</p><p>The two factors are typically:</p><ul><li><strong>Something you know:</strong> Your password</li><li><strong>Something you have:</strong> Your phone or security key</li></ul>'
